Apple today refreshed its suite of Creator Studio apps, launching the fall updates <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/27/apple-updates-creator-studio-ai-features/">that it announced in October</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1032006" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/01/Apple-Creator-Studio.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" /><br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/17/final-cut-pro-motionvfx/">Final Cut Pro with MotionVFX</a> integration is now available, letting users access MotionVFX templates, titles, themes, effects, layouts, and more right in Apple's video editing app. Timeline clips can be disconnected from the primary storyline, and there are new keyframe easing options. Apple also added royalty-free video clips to the Content Hub and a feature for quickly adjusting images in Pixelmator Pro and saving the edits in Final Cut Pro automatically.<br/>
<br/>
Logic Pro has an updated Stem Splitter with the option to break the drum stem into individual tracks, a Liquid Glass design, and Quick Look for previewing audio snapshots.<br/>
<br/>
MainStage has <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/sidecar/">Sidecar</a> support for turning the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> into a multi-touch controller, while Motion can use MotionVFX for color grading, 3D camera tracking, and visual effects. Compressor gains support for encoding videos recorded in Cinematic mode.<br/>
<br/>
Pixelmator Pro includes Generate Fill for images, taking advantage of AI for edits that blend in with surrounding content. Apple says the app can match lighting, perspective, and texture. There is a tool to circle an area to edit and improved precision for Magnetic Selection, Free Selection, and Quick Selection.<br/>
<br/>
Pages, Keynote, and Numbers include an Intelligent Assistant that can create and edit content and give guidance on using in-app tools.<br/>
<br/>
